        {
          "name": "Create user",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["users"]
            },
            "description": "Admin or HR. Creates an account and returns { user, temporaryPassword }. The temporary password is only shown in this response; the new user logs in with it and has must_change_password = true. Admins must send a role (employee, agent, hr, admin); HR can only create employees and may leave role out. department_id (an existing department) and job_title are optional. Change the email to create another account.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"New Employee\",\n  \"email\": \"new.employee@ticketflow.local\",\n  \"role\": \"employee\",\n  \"job_title\": \"Marketing Assistant\",\n  \"department_id\": 1\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Reset password",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/reset-password",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["users", "{{userId}}", "reset-password"]
            },
            "description": "Admin or HR, no body (any field is refused with 400). Gives the user a new temporary password, returned once as { user, temporaryPassword }. The old password stops working immediately, and the user must change the new one at their next login (must_change_password); sessions from before the reset are blocked until then. Admins can reset anyone but themselves (403); HR only employees. Running this changes the password of user {{userId}}."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update user",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["users", "{{userId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Send any of name, email, department_id, job_title, role, is_active (at least one); only those change, and null clears department_id and job_title. Admin: anyone, but not their own role or active status, and never the last active admin (409). HR: employee accounts only, and never role (403 even for the same value). 404 for an unknown user, 409 if the email is taken. The example keeps user 5 (Vjosa Hoxha) unchanged; try a new job_title or is_active false.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"job_title\": \"Sales Representative\",\n  \"is_active\": true,\n  \"department_id\": 1\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
